WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.534
Judge overseeing the case

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.702
against former President

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.370
Donald Trump

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.438
is now facing new scrutiny tonight

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.207
after political donations

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.609
that he made to Democrats came to light.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.811
CNN's Kara Scannell is on the story again

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.212
for us.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:12.812
Kara,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.748
these were very small contributions,

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.116
but they do raise

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.618
an important question of potential bias.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.786
What are you learning

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.156
Yeah, Alex, that's right.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.424
And some allies of the former

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.292
president are focusing in on that one

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.093
in Judge Juan

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.262
Mershon, who's overseeing this trial

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.964
to recuse himself from this case.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:31.831
So what we learn from

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.799
federal election records

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.135
is that the judge had made $35

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:38.405
in donations from in July of 2020.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.040
Those donations $15

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.541
went to the Biden campaign.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.210
$10 went to Progressive Turnout Project,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.312
and $10 went to stop Republicans.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.348
Those are two voter turnout groups.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.784
I spoke with a professor of legal ethics

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.818
and he says that

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.720
the American Bar Association

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.422
and the New York

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.523
Code of Conduct

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.223
could make

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.324
some could suggest

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.125
that some of these

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.460
donations are forbidden.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.861
But he said it's comes nowhere

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.897
close to grounds for recusal.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:04.898
We asked the court

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.433
administrators for comment.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.333
They're declining to comment

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.368
on these donations tonight.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:09.569
Alex And Kara,

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.804
the district attorney, Alvin

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.971
Bragg, is also

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:12.605
pushing back

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.207
quite forcefully on House

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.975
Republicans here in D.C.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.210
because of the pressure there

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.311
that they're putting him under.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:18.912
What's he saying

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:22.549
Yeah,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.049
I mean, there is

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.651
just been this ongoing back and forth

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.452
between the House

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.486
GOP, the House

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.387
Judiciary Chairman,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.388
Jim Jordan,

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.557
and the district attorney, Alvin Bragg.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.257
Now, tonight,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.826
Alvin Bragg has a new statement out.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.760
He has tweeted.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.227
The House

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.695
GOP continues to attempt

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.362
to undermine

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.664
an active investigation

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.699
and ongoing New York criminal case

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.434
with an unprecedented campaign

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.403
of harassment and intimidation.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.071
Repeated efforts to weaken state

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:45.572
and local

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.739
law enforcement actions

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.941
are an abuse of power

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.709
and will not deter us from our duty.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.810
To uphold the law.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.445
Now, this statement coming after Jim

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.813
Jordan have subpoenaed

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:54.814
a former prosecutor

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.282
from that office, Mark Pomeranz.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.951
Pomeranz resigned last year

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.751
after Alvin Bragg

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.953
would not authorize him

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.888
to move forward to seek an indictment

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.989
of the former president

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.224
related to the accuracy

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.692
of his financial statements.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.259
Jordan now

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.894
wanting Pomeranz to come in

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.595
for testimony.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.997
He said on April 20th deadline, and

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.199
Pomeranz is declining comment tonight.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.868
But we should note that previously

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:15.902
when Jordan asked

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.270
for this voluntary interview,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.471
he told them that

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.772
the district attorney's office

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.841
directed him to not cooperate

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.610
with their investigation. Alex.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:23.843
All right.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.811
Chris Scannell in New York,

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.512
thank you so much, Carol,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.779
for all your terrific reporting.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.614
Let's get analysis now

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.682
from our legal and political experts

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.384
Andrew McCabe, I want to start with you

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.153
and the judge's contributions

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.555
to President Biden and Democrats.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.122
It is,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:36.856
as Carol and I

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.091
were saying, a minimal amount.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:41.094
$35, but it's still not a good look

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.929
for a judge to have made these

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:43.930
donations, is it?

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:46.866
It's not a great look,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.002
Alex, but let's be honest.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.502
Do we

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.503
are we at a place

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.638
in American political life

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.706
where if you have participated in the

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.574
in the political system

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.475
at all as a voter

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.643
or a supporter of candidates

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.310
you're now

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.212
excluded from, execute

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.880
any sort of judgment or responsibility

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.981
over someone from the other party?

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.917
That seems absurd.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:04.784
You know, we have seen

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.853
many appeals of Donald

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.955
pushed by Donald Trump on many issues

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.056
in the last couple of weeks

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.524
that have been heard by judges

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.293
who he appointed to the bench.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.460
And you didn't hear any cry

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.095
for having those folks

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.163
recuse themselves

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.431
as well as they shouldn't have.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.266
So I really think at the end of the day,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.001
this is much ado about nothing.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.869
Shane, would you.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.437
Do you agree that it's absurd

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.538
or do you think the judge

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.140
there should be a conversation

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.075
about the judge recusing himself

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.579
Absolutely not.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.413
I agree with Andrew.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.214
This is absurd.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.148
Some minuscule amount.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.849
I mean, by comparison.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.619
If you look at the ridiculous

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.622
luxury trips taken in secret by Justice

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.423
Clarence Thomas,

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.325
and there is no requirement

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.460
of transparency there,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.661
what we see here,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.163
there's a requirement of transparency.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.765
The judge disclosed these contributions

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.000
if the House and Congress

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.401
want to do something constructive.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.769
Let's make the Supreme Court

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.805
disclose all these luxurious secret

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.140
gifts and trips that they take. Yeah.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.708
Those trips

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.043
and gifts from a Republican mega-donor

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.813
in an explosive new report by ProPublica.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.781
Andrew, we only have about a minute left,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.649
but I want to ask you

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.017
about what we just heard

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.119
Kara talking about attorney

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.188
that the attorney general, Alvin Bragg,

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.256
sorry, district attorney,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.824
rather, his forceful response

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.392
to those House Republicans.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.226
He called their attempts

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.562
an unprecedented campaign of harassment

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:23.963
and intimidation.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.564
What do you make of that?

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.300
I think he's exactly right.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.501
I mean, let's let's face

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.435
it, on the federal level,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.337
the Department of Justice refuses

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:31.738
often

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:32.739
gets requests

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:33.940
from Congress to go up and talk

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.575
about ongoing investigations.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.577
They routinely refuse to do so.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.711
This is a case

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.114
that is still being prosecuted

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.548
We are a long way

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.617
before any point at which the

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.052
the prosecutors

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.421
should be appearing before any sort of

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.423
congressional panel

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.924
to talk about what they're doing.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.259
I'm not sure that they ever should.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.560
And there's a state federal issue

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.361
involved here as well.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:58.197
So I believe he's on the right ground.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.032
All right.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.366
Well, we'll certainly hear more

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:03.102
I would imagine, from Congressman Jordan

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.672
in that back and forth as Shan Wu.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.406
Andrew McCabe,

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.341
thank you, as always, for your time

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.709
and your insight tonight.

